<section class="example-section">
  <p>You must now ensure everything is in place to ensure the device is secure and fully offline:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>You are running alpine on the offline device (just making sure)</li>
    <li>You removed the wifi and bluettoth chip (usually the same chip)</li>
    <li>You removed all storage drives HDD and SSD (some laptops have multiple)</li>
    <li>You unmounted the alpine boot USB and physically ejected it (see last step for instructions)</li>
    <li>You physically disconnected the ethernet cable</li>
  </ul>

  <p>At this point you should be able to do whatever you want and nothing will be persisted after a reboot because everything is running off RAM and there is no physical storage device that could persist anything even if you or malware attempted to.</p>
</section>
